* START-HISTORY:
* 18 Oct 26 dm  New, S.66.  Nine programs (and the API server) each had the clamp "kind below 1 or above 3 is 1" and the sum 12409 + kind; the
*               kinds 4 and 5 of the shared account could not be added in nine places, so the choice of text is made here, once.
* END-HISTORY
*
* START-DESCRIPTION:
*
*    deffun edit_msg(kind) calling '!edit_msg'
*    display edit_msg(kernel(K$EDIT.KIND, p))
*
* kind is what the kernel answered to K$EDIT.KIND (the EDIT_ numbers in sd.h):
*
*     1  the VOC                           12410
*     2  a dictionary                      12411
*     3  a program file                    12412
*     4  a record of a shared file         12518  (the session has not shared.write)
*     5  the structure of a shared file    12519  (SDSYS only; the kernel prints this one itself, a program only meets it when it is told)
*     anything else                        12410  (as before: an answer that is not a known kind is taken to be the VOC)
*
* It returns the TEXT, as sysmsg() does, and changes nothing.
*
* END-DESCRIPTION
*
* START-CODE

$internal
function edit_msg(kind)
$catalog !edit_msg

   begin case
      case kind = 1
         return sysmsg(12410)
      case kind = 2
         return sysmsg(12411)
      case kind = 3
         return sysmsg(12412)
      case kind = 4
         return sysmsg(12518)
      case kind = 5
         return sysmsg(12519)
   end case

   return sysmsg(12410)
end

* END-CODE
